<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehoahaz of Israel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehoahaz was king of Israel in the late 9th century BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>. According to the Bible his reign saw heavy defeats by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazael">Hazael</a> and Ben-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Hadad</a> of Aram-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, which left him with only fifty horsemen, ten <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and 10,000 foot soldiers. His son Jehoash began to recover the lost territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehoahaz-of-israel.jpg" alt="Jehoahaz of Israel" width="220" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jehoahaz_of_Israel.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
